  "limitations": [
    "Exactly one hub process owns its configuration and backend volume; no cross-process lock or multi-writer recovery is qualified.",
    "Real single-broker REST fixture validates handoff/recovery, not replicated Kafka failure tolerance.",
    "Controlled synthetic model HTTP responses validate independent capability and durable pending work, not semantic model quality.",
    "Artifact 16 covers all seven crash boundaries; artifact 17 adds alias/capability fixes and reruns hot default/no-default, partial-snapshot crash, local recovery invariants, native cases, model capability and legacy aliases. Do not attribute artifact-16 passes to artifact 17.",
    "Early Docker-wrapper artifact-15 restart observations are excluded: killing a Docker CLI does not prove the BEAM process died. Owned leftover containers were removed.",
    "CONFIG_APPLY_IN_PROGRESS is a retryable writer-domain result; parent Server/Protocol integration must publish HTTP/A2A classification before final qualification."
  ]
